    "readme_description": "There is a rectangular brick wall in front of you with `n` rows of bricks. The i<sup>th</sup> row has some number of bricks each of the same height (i.e., one unit) but they can be of different widths. The total width of each row is the same.\n\nDraw a vertical line from the top to the bottom and cross the least bricks. If your line goes through the edge of a brick, then the brick is not considered as crossed. You cannot draw a line just along one of the two vertical edges of the wall, in which case the line will obviously cross no bricks.\n\nGiven the 2D integer array `wall` that contains the information about the wall, return *the minimum number of crossed bricks after drawing such a vertical line*.",
